title: Improve Codex app-server startup feedback and lifecycle logging
updated_at: "2026-07-14T09:08:08Z"
---
The `[c2c codex app-server]` startup procedure should provide timely, unambiguous lifecycle feedback.

Requested behavior:
- Add a local `HH:MM:SS` timestamp to every log line whose prefix is `[c2c codex app-server]`, formatted as `[c2c codex app-server] [HH:MM:SS] <message>` (or the corresponding existing prefix), with the existing/appropriate color styling preserved.
- Emit a line immediately before launching the app-server so the user gets feedback before a potentially slow startup.
- Emit a line once the app-server is confirmed ready/started.
- Emit a final line immediately before the TUI takes over, including the managed agent alias/name and other useful context.

Acceptance criteria:
- Slow startup is visibly progressing rather than appearing hung.
- The three lifecycle phases (launching, ready, handing off to TUI) are distinguishable in captured output.
- Timestamp formatting and color behavior have regression coverage.